From: lich.wang <lich.wang@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: core: wait for the deferred resume before unbinding the card

snd_soc_resume() queues card->deferred_resume_work, which walks the
card's components and calls their resume callbacks.  Nothing waits for
that work when the card is unbound, so a component that goes away while
the work is running is used after it was freed.

0530 makes this reachable: q6apm_lpass_dai_resume() reopens AudioReach
graphs and waits for the DSP.  If the ADSP crashed around the suspend,
its recovery (rproc_recovery_wq is freezable, so it runs right after
thaw) unregisters the GPR devices and the q6apm DAI components while the
resume work is still waiting; the work then logs through the freed
component device and the kworker dies holding the card's locks:

  CMD timeout for [1001000] opcode
  Failed to open graph 40 in the DSP (-110)
  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 006b6e696c673a63
  pc : dev_driver_string+0x10/0x48
   _dev_err
   q6apm_graph_open
   q6apm_lpass_dai_resume
   snd_soc_component_resume
   soc_resume_deferred

Flush the work before the card loses its components: in
snd_soc_del_component_unlocked() before the component's DAIs are
unregistered, and in snd_soc_unbind_card() once card->instantiated is
clear, after which snd_soc_resume() no longer queues it.  The work only
exists on a card that was bound, so both flushes are limited to an
instantiated card.  Both unregister paths hold client_mutex; neither
soc_resume_deferred() nor any in-tree component resume callback takes
it, and no in-tree resume callback unregisters a component, so the
flush cannot wait on itself.  The cost is that an unbind racing a resume
now waits for the resume callbacks to finish (with q6apm, until its DSP
commands time out).

Link: https://github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom/issues/17
---
--- a/sound/soc/soc-core.c
+++ b/sound/soc/soc-core.c
@@ -823,10 +823,24 @@
 	/* deferred resume work */
 	INIT_WORK(&card->deferred_resume_work, soc_resume_deferred);
 }
+
+/*
+ * The deferred resume work walks the card's components and calls their
+ * resume callbacks, which may wait on firmware (an AudioReach graph open
+ * waits for the DSP).  A component can be unregistered meanwhile, e.g. when
+ * the DSP that hosts it restarts, so wait for the work before the card
+ * loses its components.  Only valid on a card that was bound, as the work
+ * is initialised at bind time.
+ */
+static void soc_resume_flush(struct snd_soc_card *card)
+{
+	flush_work(&card->deferred_resume_work);
+}
 #else
 #define snd_soc_suspend NULL
 #define snd_soc_resume NULL
 static inline void soc_resume_init(struct snd_soc_card *card) { }
+static inline void soc_resume_flush(struct snd_soc_card *card) { }
 #endif
 
 static struct device_node
@@ -1996,6 +2010,9 @@
 {
 	if (snd_soc_card_is_instantiated(card)) {
 		card->instantiated = false;
+
+		/* snd_soc_resume() no longer queues the work once this is clear */
+		soc_resume_flush(card);
 
 		snd_soc_remove_device_links(card);
 
@@ -2694,6 +2711,10 @@
 {
 	struct snd_soc_card *card = component->card;
 	bool instantiated;
+
+	/* a running resume may still use this component's DAIs */
+	if (card && snd_soc_card_is_instantiated(card))
+		soc_resume_flush(card);
 
 	snd_soc_unregister_dais(component);
 
